From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:03:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/48] net: airoha: xpon: restore OMCI GEM ports under
 gem_mib_lock

"let Encrypted_Port-ID restore GEM ports OMCI created" decided to
restore a port under gem_mib_lock, dropped the lock and then rewrote the
port through __gpon_set_gem_port_hw(). An OMCI delete in that window
would have been undone by the PLOAM message. Do the test and the write
under one hold of the lock with a new __gpon_set_gem_port_hw_locked().

That commit also presented the restore as something the field link
needed. It only matters where the GEM table is lost between sessions
(EN7523 resets its MAC at session start, or gpon_stop_clear_gems /
gpon_stop_mac_reset are set); on the EN751221 with the defaults the
ports are still in the table and nothing changed. The comment now says
so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 42 ++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 09c9977..7690dfd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -1354,17 +1354,14 @@ static void gpon_mib_start(struct xpon_priv *priv)
  * update of encrypted_gems, so a concurrent Encrypted_Port-ID cannot be
  * overwritten by an OMCI write that sampled the bitmap before it.
  */
-static int __gpon_set_gem_port_hw(struct xpon_priv *priv, u16 gem_port_id,
-				  bool valid, bool encrypted,
-				  bool ploam_encryption)
+static int __gpon_set_gem_port_hw_locked(struct xpon_priv *priv,
+					 u16 gem_port_id, bool valid,
+					 bool encrypted, bool ploam_encryption)
 {
 	bool was;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (gem_port_id >= GPON_MAX_GEM_ID)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
-	mutex_lock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+	lockdep_assert_held(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
 	if (valid && ploam_encryption &&
 	    test_bit(gem_port_id, priv->encrypted_gems))
 		encrypted = true;
@@ -1379,6 +1376,22 @@ static int __gpon_set_gem_port_hw(struct xpon_priv *priv, u16 gem_port_id,
 		if (priv->gem_mib_enabled)
 			gpon_mib_rebuild_locked(priv);
 	}
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int __gpon_set_gem_port_hw(struct xpon_priv *priv, u16 gem_port_id,
+				  bool valid, bool encrypted,
+				  bool ploam_encryption)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	if (gem_port_id >= GPON_MAX_GEM_ID)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	mutex_lock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+	ret = __gpon_set_gem_port_hw_locked(priv, gem_port_id, valid,
+					    encrypted, ploam_encryption);
 	mutex_unlock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
 
 	return ret;
@@ -2359,17 +2372,20 @@ static int gpon_cb_set_gem_encryption(void *hw_priv, u16 port_id,
 	configured = test_bit(port_id, priv->hw_gems);
 	/*
 	 * A port OMCI created and has not deleted, but which is missing from
-	 * the GEM table (a MAC reset at session start on EN7523), is put back
-	 * as before: when the OLT skips OMCI provisioning after a reactivation
-	 * this message is what restores it.
+	 * the GEM table, is put back as before: when the OLT skips OMCI
+	 * provisioning after a reactivation this message is what restores
+	 * it. That only happens where the GEM table is lost between sessions
+	 * (EN7523 MAC reset at start, gpon_stop_clear_gems, gpon_stop_mac_reset);
+	 * on the EN751221 with the defaults the port is still "configured".
 	 */
 	restore = !configured && test_bit(port_id, priv->omci_gems);
 	if (configured)
 		ret = gpon_write_gem_port_hw(priv, port_id, true, encrypted);
+	else if (restore)
+		/* Under the same lock: OMCI cannot delete it in between. */
+		ret = __gpon_set_gem_port_hw_locked(priv, port_id, true,
+						    encrypted, true);
 	mutex_unlock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
-	if (restore)
-		ret = __gpon_set_gem_port_hw(priv, port_id, true, encrypted,
-					     true);
 
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(priv->dev,
